    "created_at": "2021-01-06T07:13:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-01-06T07:13:57Z",
    "body": "I don't see Paul mentioning that? In any event, given that we expose events in audio worklets, it seems we should expose this as otherwise `addEventListener()` is less functional in audio worklets and that would be confusing.\r\n\r\n(If you want other APIs to adopt this as well, typically you would make them accept a dictionary with a `signal` member, as `addEventListener()` and `fetch()` do, for instance.)",
